From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:01:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: say in the kernel log how each HDMI mode set goes
 out

Two reports of a picture lost behind an AV receiver on Intel graphics: issue
#28 (corgeone: i7-1355U, Anthem AVM 90, LG G2) and siriusbox in the LibreELEC
forum (thread 30362, #797 and #798: an ASRock B660 board, a Sony HT-A9, a
Hisense projector over TMDS), who loses the picture leaving the BIOS and when
an HDR10 film starts at 10 bits, never with Dolby Vision (8 bits). Which of
the mode sets were scrambled, at which TMDS clock and depth, is what tells
those cases apart, and i915 said it only in its debug output.

intel_ddi_enable_hdmi() now says it at info level for each HDMI mode set:
"[CONNECTOR:...] HDMI mode set: 3840x2160 at 24 Hz, TMDS clock 445500 kHz,
RGB at 12 bpc, scrambling yes, TMDS bit clock ratio 1/40", as NVKMS does on
NVIDIA (nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9044). One line per mode set; nothing else
changes.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
index e0f2a4f..f3396f1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 #include "intel_crtc.h"
 #include "intel_cx0_phy.h"
 #include "intel_cx0_phy_regs.h"
+#include "intel_crtc_state_dump.h"
 #include "intel_ddi.h"
 #include "intel_ddi_buf_trans.h"
 #include "intel_de.h"
@@ -3496,6 +3497,22 @@ static void intel_ddi_enable_hdmi(struct intel_atomic_state *state,
 	WRITE_ONCE(to_intel_connector(connector)->output_set_up_at, jiffies);
 	WRITE_ONCE(to_intel_connector(connector)->output_set_up, true);
 
+	/*
+	 * Hades: how the HDMI link of each mode set goes out, as NVKMS says it on NVIDIA
+	 * (nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9044): what an AV receiver or a display that loses the
+	 * picture at some mode changes takes, and does not (issue #28, and a Sony HT-A9 to a
+	 * projector that loses it at 10 bits and not with Dolby Vision at 8)
+	 */
+	drm_info(display->drm,
+		 "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] HDMI mode set: %dx%d%s at %d Hz, TMDS clock %d kHz, %s at %d bpc, scrambling %s, TMDS bit clock ratio 1/%d\n",
+		 connector->base.id, connector->name,
+		 crtc_state->hw.adjusted_mode.hdisplay, crtc_state->hw.adjusted_mode.vdisplay,
+		 crtc_state->hw.adjusted_mode.flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_INTERLACE ? "i" : "",
+		 drm_mode_vrefresh(&crtc_state->hw.adjusted_mode), crtc_state->port_clock,
+		 intel_output_format_name(crtc_state->output_format), crtc_state->pipe_bpp / 3,
+		 str_yes_no(crtc_state->hdmi_scrambling),
+		 crtc_state->hdmi_high_tmds_clock_ratio ? 40 : 10);
+
 	if (has_buf_trans_select(display))
 		hsw_prepare_hdmi_ddi_buffers(encoder, crtc_state);
 
-- 
